bcarlisle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T04:04:25Z","updated_at":"2024-12-30T04:04:25Z","body":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/2ed4d65af0a1993c0df7b081f4088d0f3614283e/aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/ChannelShuffleKernel.cpp#L25\r\n\r\nThis is due to calculating the number of channels per group. Division by 0 error. I think it is safe to assume that we should probably have at least 1 group. So maybe we need to let the user know that groups has to be > 0???  Maybe log a warning and then don't actually shuffle, just return the tensor that was passed in?\r\n\r\nThe documentation doesn't mention anything about valid ranges for the groups input range. Unless I am blind and couldn't find it.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2565003223/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"abcarlisle","id":156453508,"node_id":"U_kgDOCVNKhA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/156453508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle","html_url":"https://github.com/abcarlisle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abcarlisle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":